####################################################################
# cat1b_asystole_ibp.dlog — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# NL rule (CAT1): "If an asystole alarm occurs when an invasive blood
# pressure sensor is present without alarms on that sensing pathway, it may
# be flagged as likely false positive."
#
# Clause by clause (decisions agreed 2026-09-21):
#   "an asystole alarm"        — the arriving alarm's OWN metric (?gT, its
#                                transient graph) is a heart rate with an
#                                absent rhythm. Never read from another
#                                alarm's graph: that let e.g. "Lage
#                                hartfreq." be flagged while an asystole
#                                was active.
#   "an invasive blood         — an ARTERIAL transducer (sensor:
#    pressure sensor"            ABP_transducer) on the IBP functional unit
#                                of a PATIENT MONITOR (device:
#                                PhysiologicalMonitor or a subclass: Philips,
#                                Draeger, ...). Deliberately narrower than
#                                the NL wording, which should read
#                                "invasive ARTERIAL blood pressure": ECMO
#                                circuit pressures (CARDIOHELP pArt/pVen) and
#                                venous pressure do not show that the heart
#                                is beating — on VA-ECMO a real asystole
#                                coexists with a stable pressure.
#   "is present"               — observable only through the line's own
#                                alarms: an IBP alarm's persistent graph
#                                (?gIbp, holding the whole patient -> device
#                                -> functional unit -> transducer chain)
#                                remains valid until 15 minutes after that
#                                alarm ended (ontology.ttl's
#                                postAlarmValidityDuration). After 15 minutes
#                                of silence the line is no longer known to be
#                                there, and an asystole is not flagged — the
#                                safe error for a rule that downgrades one.
#   "without alarms on that    — literally: no currently valid alarm is
#    sensing pathway"            triggered by that IBP functional unit
#                                (NOT EXISTS). The earlier version checked
#                                the pathway's reported states instead
#                                (operation state, quality, metric value) —
#                                equivalent only as long as every IBP alarm
#                                asserts one of the listed bad states, and
#                                satisfied by any one healthy value when a
#                                criterion had several.
#   "it may be flagged"        — flagged at onset, and WITHDRAWN if an alarm
#                                on that same IBP pathway arrives while the
#                                asystole is still active: in a genuine
#                                asystole the pressure alarm follows the ECG
#                                alarm by seconds. The withdrawal is not
#                                expressible as a rule here — it is a stored
#                                flag plus a delete; see replay_driver.py's
#                                cat1_flag_insert/cat1b_withdraw.
#
# NOT LOADED AS A STANDING RULE: it runs as a one-shot `select` (and the
# flag INSERT) at each alarm's arrival, hand-translated into
# engine/replay_driver.py's _ONDEMAND_BODY_TEMPLATES["cat1b"]. Negation is
# written in SPARQL form below (NOT EXISTS is query-only), so this file
# documents the logic in the project's bracket-quad style rather than being
# loadable Datalog. Keep the two in sync by hand; the cat1b_* fixtures
# check both.
####################################################################

@prefix mda:              <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix mdapoc:           <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#> .
@prefix rdfs:             <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix metric:           <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric/> .
@prefix metricRhythm:     <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rhythm/> .
@prefix functionalUnit:   <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/functional-unit/> .
@prefix sensor:           <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/sensor/> .
@prefix device:           <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/device/> .

[?alarm, mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive, ?ibpFunctionalUnit] ?gT :-
    # an asystole alarm (its own metric)
    [?alarm, mda:hasMessage, ?msg] ?gT,
    [?msg, mda:concernsPatient, ?patient] ?gT,
    [?analysis, mda:producesMetric, ?metric] ?gT,
    [?metric, rdf:type, metric:HeartRate] ?gT,
    [?metric, mda:hasRhythm, metricRhythm:Absent] ?gT,
    # an arterial line on a patient monitor, known present
    [?patient, mda:isMonitoredBy, ?ibpDevice] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpDevice, rdf:type, ?ibpDeviceType] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpDevice, mda:hasFunctionalUnit, ?ibpFunctionalUnit] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpFunctionalUnit, rdf:type, functionalUnit:FU_InvasiveBloodPressure] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpFunctionalUnit, mda:hasSensor, ?ibpSensor] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpSensor, rdf:type, sensor:ABP_transducer] ?gIbp,
    [?ibpDeviceType, rdfs:subClassOf*, device:PhysiologicalMonitor],
    # without a current alarm on that pathway
    NOT EXISTS ?other, ?otherMsg, ?gOther IN (
        [?other, mda:hasMessage, ?otherMsg] ?gOther,
        [?otherMsg, mda:triggeredBy, ?ibpFunctionalUnit] ?gOther ) .

# VALIDATION — engine/replay_driver.py run(), fixtures in
# DATA/CAT_evaluation/events_data.csv: cat1b_pos (arterial line alarmed 10
# min earlier) and cat1b_other_monitor (arterial line on a Draeger monitor)
# flag; cat1b_neg (arterial line alarming now) and cat1b_ecmo (ECMO circuit
# pressure only) do not; cat1b_withdraw is flagged and withdrawn when the
# arterial line alarms 8 s after onset; cat1b_borrow flags the asystole but
# not a heart-rate alarm arriving during it.
